{"Backup code invalidation is not atomic: two concurrent login requests can both decrypt the same backup code list, find the same code, and each perform an update, allowing a single backup code to be used multiple times": 0.9663740396499634, "The 'continue' button in the confirm-password step has type='submit' while also calling handleSetup on onClick, causing both handleSetup and the form's handleEnable to fire, resulting in an unintended enable submission with empty TOTP code and double network calls": 0.49169066548347473, "The password visibility toggle button has tabIndex={-1}, which removes it from the tab order and prevents keyboard users from focusing and activating it, breaking accessibility for non-mouse users": 0.9733328819274902}